# Revision code: 5320 - 2013-03-27
#
# The format of an ASCII mesh file is defined as follows:
#
# a)  OPTIONAL:
#     Some comments (like the one you are just reading).
#     Each comment line must be preceded by a '#'.
#
# b)  A section defining the MANDATORY mesh information, i.e.
#     vertex coordinates and the vertex indices per triangle:
# b1) Initial identifier 'OFF1' or 'OFF2' (tetrahedra, line segments).
# b2) Three integers [in one line] corresponding to:
#     NumVtx NumTri EmptyField (still to be defined)
# b3) The vertex coordinates [in mm]  [one line per vertex]
#     with x-direction going from right to left
#          y-direction going from back to front
#          z-direction going from head to foot.
# b4) The triangle definition         [one line per triangle]
#     Initial entry 3 (= number of vertices) followed by
#     the vertex indices corresponding to each triangle.
#
# c)  OPTIONAL (if using identifier 'OFF2'):
#     List of tetrahedra: Section defining the indices of vertices
#     and optionally also of "valid" triangles of all tetrahedra:
# c1) Version with vertex indices only:
#     - Initial identifier 'TETRAHEDRON_VERTEX_SPECIFICATION'
#     - Initial line with an integer -> number of tetrahedra
#     - So many lines with 4 integers [one line per tetrah.]
#       indices of the 4 vertices defining the tetrahedron
# c2) Version with vertex indices and triangle indices:
#     - Initial identifier
#       'TETRAHEDRON_VERTEX_AND_TRIANGLE_SPECIFICATION'
#     - Initial line with an integer -> number of tetrahedra
#     - So many lines with >= 5 integers [one line per tet.]
#       indices of the 4 vertices defining the tetrahedron;
#       thereafter the number of "valid" triangles from b4)
#       followed by so many indices of the corresp. triangles
#       (these will be checked while reading the file ...)
#
# d)  OPTIONAL (if using identifier 'OFF2'):
#     List of line segments: Section defining the indices of vertices
#     - Initial identifier 'LINE_SEGMENTS'
#     - Initial line with an integer -> number of line segments
#     - So many lines with 2 integers [one line per line segment.]
#       indices of the 2 vertices defining the line segment
#
# e)  OPTIONAL:
#     Section defining neighbors for vertices and triangles:
# e1) Initial identifier 'FAST_MODEL_LOADING'
# e2) Vertex neighbors                [one line per vertex]
#     Initial entry = number of neighbors, followed by the
#     indices of the neighbor vertices
# e3) Triangle neighbors              [two lines per triangle]
#     Initial entry of first line
#     = number of all vertex-connected neighbor triangles,
#     followed by indices of these neighbor triangles.
#     Initial entry of second line
#     = number of all edge-connected neighbor triangles,
#     followed by indices of these neighbor triangles.
#
# f)  OPTIONAL:
#     Section defining some "valid" volume (in the form of a
#     bounding box) and its relation to the mesh coordinates:
# f1) Initial identifier 'VOLUME_INFORMATION'
# f2) Identifier 'BOUNDING_BOX'
# f3) Coordinates of the bounding box [in mm] (6 doubles):
#     MinX MinY MinZ
#     MaxX MaxY MaxZ
# f4) Identifier 'MESH_TRANSLATION'
# f5) Translation vector [in mm] (3 doubles) to be applied
#     to all coordinates to shift the mesh into the defined
#     bounding box (e.g. to identify out-of-volume regions):
#     ShiftX ShiftY ShiftZ
